# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded reciprocal square root 1 / sqrt(x) of BF16
#
# 1 / sqrt(2^e m) = (1 / sqrt(2^e)) (1 / sqrt(m)): the exponent part and the 128 mantissas in [1, 2) are both
# tabulated as B32 values whose product rounds correctly to BF16, and subnormals have a table of their own. Round to
# nearest only: +0 gives +inf, -0 gives -inf, +inf gives +0, a negative x gives NaN, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/rsqrt/rsqrt_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module System/Numerics/BF16

